  "notes": [
    "Regular -AR verb — follows standard -AR endings with no exceptions",
    "Past participle: *marchado* (regular)",
    "Means \"to march\" (soldiers, a parade) — *los soldados marchan en fila* (the soldiers march in formation) — or, informally, \"to go/run\" (a machine, a plan, a situation): *¿cómo marcha el proyecto?* (how's the project going?), *el motor marcha bien* (the engine is running well)",
    "Reflexive *marcharse* means \"to leave/go away,\" very common in everyday speech: *me marcho a casa* (I'm heading home)",
    "Related: *marcha* (march, gear — as in a car; also \"nightlife/atmosphere\" colloquially: *tiene mucha marcha* = it has a lot of energy/life), *marchoso/a* (colloquial, \"fun-loving/into the nightlife\")"
  ],
